  <h2>What HEVC is</h2>
  <p>HEVC, also called H.265, is a video format that keeps about the same picture in a smaller file than the older H.264. Phones and capture tools use it to save space:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>iPhones, with <b>High Efficiency</b> chosen in the camera's formats (the default).</li>
    <li>Many Android phones, when set to save space.</li>
    <li>The NVIDIA app, OBS and other recorders, when set to H.265 or HEVC.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The file's name doesn't say which format is inside: an <code>.mp4</code> or <code>.mov</code> can be either.</p>

  <h2>Which formats play in the chat</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>H.264</b> plays in the chat on every computer and phone. It is the safe choice.</li>
    <li><b>HEVC</b> keeps more detail at the same size, and plays on most phones and newer computers, but may not on older ones.</li>
    <li><b>AV1</b> keeps the most detail at the same size, and plays on computers, but may not on phones.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Convert it</h2>
  <p><a href={u()}>Sub20</a> encodes H.264 unless you choose otherwise, so dropping the video on it and pressing <b>Compress</b> is enough. It fits the result under the size you pick (20 MB to start), so it sends on a free account too.</p>
  <p>Sub20 offers HEVC and AV1 as well, and says where you pick them which devices may not play them.</p>
  <p>Without installing anything, <a href={u("app/")}>Sub20 Lite</a> converts to H.264 in the browser. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
